lit-xlsx was written for this repository. No file, function or passage was copied from another project. Its design
borrows techniques from the sources below, rewritten in its own words and code:

- anthropics/skills, skills/xlsx (Apache License 2.0, https://github.com/anthropics/skills):
  recalculating in LibreOffice with a separate user profile, the list of formula error values, the _xlfn prefix rule
  for newer functions, openpyxl pitfalls, and the input/formula/link colour convention.
- anthropics/financial-services, financial-analysis audit-xls skill (Apache License 2.0,
  https://github.com/anthropics/financial-services): an audit that reports findings by severity before changing
  anything, hardcodes inside formulas, a case switch with INDEX, and a Checks sheet.
- openai/skills, skills/.curated/spreadsheet at commit e6afb0d (Apache License 2.0, https://github.com/openai/skills):
  rendering each sheet through LibreOffice and Poppler and looking at it before delivery.
- proxlsx-skill by the same author: a named-role builder, lint rules against default sheet names, General number
  formats and too many fills, and templates built from a single script.

Runtime dependencies are installed on first use and are not bundled: openpyxl (MIT), XlsxWriter (BSD-2-Clause),
defusedxml (PSF-2.0), lxml (BSD-3-Clause), Pillow (MIT-CMU). LibreOffice and Poppler are host tools that are only detected.
